1
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,400
Pair of jokers.

2
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,400
What are you doing?

3
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,240
Hello, aunties.

4
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,120
Hello, aunties.

5
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,760
Ranran.

6
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,040
You have a guest.

7
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:51,840
Ranran.

8
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,240
I brought your favorite roses.

9
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,440
And soup.

10
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,320
Who's a guest?

11
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:03,600
Zhuang Qiang.

12
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,920
Don't you understand what I'm saying?

13
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,280
Take your stuff and get the hell out.

14
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:07,880
Ranran.

15
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,160
Try my stewed pork trotters.

16
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:10,320
They're delicious.

17
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,080
They smell so good.

18
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:16,040
Here.

19
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:16,640
Ranran.

20
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:17,440
Have a taste.

21
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,360
They melt in your mouth.

22
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,160
If they melt in your mouth,

23
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,000
why don't you get lost?

24
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,360
I made them just for you.

25
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,720
Stewed them for over three hours.

26
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:25,320
Try them.

27
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:26,920
The doctor ordered

28
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,960
a light diet after surgery.

29
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,000
No greasy food.

30
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:31,840
Ranran.

31
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:32,600
Mine is

32
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,640
rich in protein,

33
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,640
and good for recovery.

34
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:35,560
It's delicious.

35
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,320
Come on.

36
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:36,800
Try some.

37
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,040
Sister Lan, which one do you prefer?

38
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,520
If you ask me, Little Chen is better.

39
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,920
That other kid isn't much to look at.

40
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,320
And he seems a bit dumb.

41
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:50,240
Yours is burnt, isn't it?

42
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:50,840
Here, Yiran.

43
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,720
Eat mine.

44
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:55,760
Ranran.

45
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,040
This is too plain.

46
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,960
And it's overcooked.

47
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,120
Leave it if you can't finish.

48
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,560
Small, frequent meals are good for the stomach.

49
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,720
You should go back first.

50
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,840
I have some family matters to deal with.

51
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,160
Such a good show,

52
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,120
I have to keep watching.

53
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,560
Zhang Lijuan.

54
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,280
Then I'll watch it next time.

55
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,360
I'm going to buy a fish head for soup.

56
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,040
Ranran.

57
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:30,840
You used to

58
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,760
love my stewed pork trotters the most.

59
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,040
That was before.

60
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,600
I don't like them anymore.

61
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,120
Who are you?

62
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,160
Can't you tell what my relationship with her is?

63
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,440
We were together for so many years.

64
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,400
Who the hell are you?

65
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,080
Then can't you see

66
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,360
what her body language says right now?

67
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,560
Ranran.

68
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:58,920
Who are you?

69
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,560
Who are you?

70
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,600
He asked who you are.

71
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,920
Me.

72
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:11,440
I'm Li Yiran's mom.

73
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,560
Auntie!

74
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,040
Want some pork trotters?

75
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,040
They melt in your mouth.

76
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:21,640
Too greasy.

77
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:22,280
Hold this.

78
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,840
This tie is quite nice.

79
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:27,520
Yeah.

80
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,560
Imported from Italy.

81
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,320
Pretty expensive.

82
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,800
Come on, step outside for a bit.

83
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:32,240
Auntie.

84
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,280
Don't shout. Don't shout.

85
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,720
Auntie!

86
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,200
Ow, ow, ow!

87
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,120
You're coming with me!

88
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:45,320
How about

89
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:46,880
having some soup?

90
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,400
Throw that away.

91
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,280
This...

92
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:58,960
You had chopsticks.

93
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,000
But you didn't give them to me earlier.

94
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,400
They're his.

95
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:02,960
Then I won't use them.

96
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,040
You want to eat it?

97
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,000
My cooking is pretty good, right?

98
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:21,640
You made this?

99
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,560
I made it.

100
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:45,240
Are you hungry?

101
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,040
I made you some fish soup.

102
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,440
Who was it that said earlier

103
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,160
I couldn't eat meat or fish?

104
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,840
Well, that depends

105
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:55,840
on who made it.

106
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,320
Where's Wu Huilian?

107
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,440
She was at the hospital for three days,

108
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,440
so I told her to go home and rest.

109
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,360
I'll just leave it here

110
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,160
to let it cool.

111
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,160
By the way,

112
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,520
that tattooed guy from the other day

113
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,720
was caught by the police.

114
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,360
He confessed to all his crimes.

115
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,800
The police followed the leads

116
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,720
and caught the other suspects.

117
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,480
Now we just wait for the trial.

118
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,040
That's great.

119
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,280
Xizi's spirit in heaven

120
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,680
can finally rest in peace.

121
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,280
You should go home and rest too.

122
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,640
Look how tired you are.

123
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,720
Don't worry, I can manage by myself.

124
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:45,520
No way.

125
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,080
I have to stay with you.

126
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:51,720
Alright.

127
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,240
Just pour me a little bit.

128
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,560
It'll cool faster.

129
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:33,080
Welcome home!

130
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,680
Welcome, welcome!

131
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,160
Oh my gosh!

132
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:45,320
Welcome home! Welcome home!

133
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,480
Okay, okay, okay.

134
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,480
You scared me to death!

135
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,680
I thought something had happened.

136
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,480
Everything's fine.

137
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:02,320
Let's welcome our heroine home from the hospital!

138
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,360
Thanks, Yangyang.

139
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,760
Yiran!

140
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,720
Auntie Juan!

141
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,920
I'm just glad you're okay. You're finally back.

142
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,080
Heroine! Heroine!

143
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,600
Ranran!

144
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,840
What's the meaning of this?

145
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:29,680
Ranran.

146
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,520
Can I have a breakup dinner with you?

147
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,280
Is that okay?

148
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,680
Let's part on good terms.

149
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:47,560
Come on.

150
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:50,640
Let's go, let's go.

151
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,800
We're leaving, let's go, let's go.

152
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:11,920
Go ahead.

153
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,200
What else do you have to say?

154
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,160
Get it all out right now.

155
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,240
We said this is a breakup dinner.

156
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:19,920
Why are you still being so serious?

157
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:22,640
I know.

158
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,680
You're someone who hates dragging things out.

159
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,640
I shouldn't say anything to try and make you stay.

160
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,760
Today, I just want to tell you...

161
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,840
We both came from small towns.

162
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:35,920
Shanghai is just too big.

163
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,520
It's so easy to lose your way.

164
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:40,360
If I had nothing to lean on,

165
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,080
I really couldn't stay.

166
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:46,960
If you're still making excuses even now,

167
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,520
there's really no need.

168
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,160
Oh, by the way.

169
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,760
Your mom came to see me.

170
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,040
Wu Huilian.

171
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,360
What did she want with you?

172
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,040
It was right here.

173
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,400
She dragged me over here.

174
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,400
Sorry about earlier.

175
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,240
I was a little rude.

176
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,160
It's fine, Auntie.

177
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,080
Actually, I

178
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,600
was also very impolite.

179
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:15,200
Did Yiran ever tell you about her family?

180
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,800
Not really.

181
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,680
She just said her dad passed away.

182
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:19,600
What about her mom?

183
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,800
I didn't dare ask.

184
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,000
She'd get mad whenever I asked.

185
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,120
Alright then.

186
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,120
Let me tell you about it.

187
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,680
Eight years ago,

188
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,760
right in this very spot,

189
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,800
her Pops and I ran a food stall.

190
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,440
One night,

191
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:39,560
some thugs were bullying a little girl.

192
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,560
I couldn't just stand by and watch,

193
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,160
so I started fighting them,

194
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:46,000
and almost got myself killed.

195
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,760
Just when I was in serious danger,

196
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,280
her Pops came back from delivering takeout.

197
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,440
Her Pops came over to help me.

198
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,800
But the thugs, using their numbers,

199
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,040
beat her Pops half to death.

200
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:04,720
In a moment of impulse,

201
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:07,440
I grabbed a nearby knife,

202
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,720
and rushed at their leader.

203
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,480
With just a few strikes,

204
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:15,600
that man was dead.

205
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,520
I spent eight years on the inside.

206
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,440
And Yiran spent eight years on the outside.

207
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,440
For these eight years,

208
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,760
she hasn't had a single family member by her side.

209
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,600
You are her first love,

210
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,680
and once the person she trusted most.

211
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,360
I know all about what happened between you two.

212
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:40,920
What you want,

213
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,280
Yiran can't give you.

214
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,880
And what she wants,

215
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,000
you can't give her either.

216
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:48,960
As for me,

217
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,240
I only want one thing.

218
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:52,240
I want her to be happy.

219
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,400
Zhuang.

220
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,200
Yiran is my entire world.

221
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:04,640
If anyone tries to bully her,

222
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:07,040
I'm not afraid of going back inside again.

223
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,920
The thing between you two is over now.

224
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:11,600
Let her go,

225
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,320
and you'll be freeing yourself, too.

226
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,280
With this drink,

227
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:17,080
Auntie toasts you.

228
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,440
Here.

229
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:24,800
Yiran,

230
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,320
even though we can't be together anymore,

231
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,080
can we still be friends?

232
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,480
We're both adults now.

233
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:38,840
There's no need to be so sentimental.

234
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,640
May our paths

235
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,520
never cross again.

236
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,400
Why are you back?

237
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,240
I...

238
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,720
I didn't even cook for you.

239
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:04,120
I grabbed a bowl of rice noodles on the street.

240
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,120
I'm not hungry.

241
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,040
Ran... uh... ate...

242
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:10,600
I ate too much.

243
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,680
Went for a run to digest it.

244
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,360
I'm a little thirsty.

245
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:17,600
Let's go.

246
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,360
I'll make you tea when we get back. Let's go.

247
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,760
You just got out of the hospital and you went running?

248
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:25,960
You're gonna shake your head until you pass out.

249
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:39,960
Hello, Mr. Wang.

250
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,960
About what we discussed, you really can't offer a discount?

251
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,600
We've worked together for so long.

252
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Please do me a favor.

253
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,680
Mr. Zhou,

254
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:50,000
I really had no choice last time.

255
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,600
I'll lose money if I lower the price.

256
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,320
Then can we meet and talk?

257
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,040
To see exactly where

258
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,680
we can further cut costs.

259
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,880
What are you doing?

260
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,720
Xiao... Xiaofang.

261
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:28,680
Do you think our water is free?

262
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,040
Why are you back?

263
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,440
Can't I come back to my own home?

264
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,280
Let me wash these.

265
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,320
You've been working hard all day.

266
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,920
Go get some rest.

267
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:42,640
Go on.

268
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,520
How are things on your end?

269
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,800
The unit cost overrun isn't much,

270
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,760
but the volume is huge this time.

271
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:30,760
Running the total, it's 30% over budget!

272
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,760
Don't we still have cash in the company account?

273
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,280
My dear young Master Zhou,

274
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:39,240
Do you know how much the company's monthly rent, utilities,

275
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:42,480
payroll, and social security cost in total?

276
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,280
We're already operating at a loss.

277
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:45,800
Now with Mr. Wang raising his prices...

278
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,600
Why did he suddenly raise his prices?

279
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,520
Boss, you're using all high-end custom models.

280
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,000
Mr. Wang absolutely won't lower his prices.

281
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,360
I put all our cash flow into the products

282
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,120
just to maintain our reputation.

283
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,920
Who knew he'd pull a stunt like this?

284
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,480
Business is all about profit.

285
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,200
There's no room for sentiment.

286
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,000
We either cut the service quality...

287
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:09,880
I'm not cutting the quality.

288
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,120
Besides, cutting the quality is useless.

289
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,840
If the clients aren't satisfied,

290
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:14,880
our reputation takes a hit,

291
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:15,840
and all our hard work goes down the drain.

292
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:18,080
Then how about...

293
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,600
we ask Mr. Zhou Senior for help?

294
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:23,320
Even if I have to tough it out alone,

295
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,320
I'll never ask him for help.

296
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:28,840
Isn't she lovely?

297
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:29,680
She is.

298
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:30,800
Beautiful, right?

299
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:31,680
Beautiful.

300
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:33,760
Her name is Li Yiran.

301
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:35,040
She's my daughter.

302
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:37,400
She graduated from a top university in Shanghai.

303
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,160
Such class.

304
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,440
People who've lived in the big city are just different.

305
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:44,000
She even worked for a Fortune 500 company.

306
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,520
A Fortune 500 company?

307
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:48,240
Wouldn't she have hundreds of people under her?

308
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:49,840
Do you want to exhaust her?

309
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,000
Managing that many people!

310
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,120
Though she did manage a small team.

311
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,520
Now, for my sake,

312
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:56,320
she came back to this little town.

313
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,640
That head of hers

314
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,480
is incredibly sharp.

315
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:01,080
She inherited all my good genes.

316
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,920
Then her boyfriend must be pretty amazing too, right?

317
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:04,320
What's wrong with you?

318
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,320
Always rubbing salt in my wounds!

319
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,040
She has high standards.

320
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,960
She hasn't found anyone she likes yet.

321
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,760
Should we set her up with someone?

322
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,760
She's seen the big wide world.

323
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,240
How could she settle for someone from our little town?

324
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,480
No way.

325
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,920
What do you guys mean?

326
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:30,400
Gathering intel in a town this small!

327
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:33,360
The company is going bankrupt!

328
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,040
The company is going bankrupt!

329
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,240
When did you get back?

330
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:58,120
Zoning out?

331
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:08,720
You said before

332
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,880
that I was a whatchamacallit...

333
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:12,600
Whatever industry I join, it goes under.

334
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,760
What was it?

335
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,920
What kind of jinx?

336
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,320
Industry jinx.

337
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:16,800
Right.

338
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,000
It really is

339
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:20,640
so damn frustrating.

340
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:22,680
Before, I

341
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,000
went to an escape room

342
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,760
to work as an NPC.

343
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,200
I moved bricks,

344
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,040
and carried frozen pork.

345
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,840
I did a bunch of random jobs.

346
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,760
And they all went out of business.

347
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,560
Even when I went to sell fish,

348
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,640
I only did it for a bit,

349
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:40,120
and the next day, the boss stopped selling fish

350
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:41,280
and switched to selling yarn.

351
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,200
Selling yarn?

352
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:44,480
No.

353
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,480
Actually, let me tell you,

354
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:47,920
I really like working at Joy Bells.

355
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,080
Being there...

356
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,880
I'm actually pretty happy.

357
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,080
You're saying all this...

358
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:56,200
Did something happen to Joy Bells?

359
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:59,280
The ship of Joy Bells

360
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:01,680
has crashed into me, the industry jinx.

361
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:05,320
I'm afraid it's really going to sink.

362
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,280
Don't overthink it right now.

363
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:08,880
I think,

364
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,720
even if Joy Bells goes under...

365
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,920
Bite your tongue!

366
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:14,040
You jinx, knock on wood three times!

367
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,640
You're that superstitious?

368
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:20,480
Then I'll go get that fraud from before

369
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:22,160
to light a candle in the southeast corner for you.

370
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,440
If I ever believe that fraud again,

371
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,960
I'll eat shit.

372
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:32,000
Actually, I don't think you need to be so anxious.

373
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,280
Think about it.

374
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:35,920
You've already made a name for yourself

375
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:36,840
as a top matchmaker.

376
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,960
Whichever matchmaking agency you go to,

377
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,400
wouldn't they all want you?

378
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:45,640
It's mainly that right now,

379
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,760
I can't bear to leave Boss Zhou

380
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:49,640
and Wumei's gang.

381
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:51,960
At first, I sort of

382
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,120
couldn't stand them.

383
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:56,480
Who knew that as we spent time together,

384
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,880
I'd get so attached to them, you know?

385
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,880
They are pretty good people.

386
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,240
This is so damn annoying!

387
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:16,840
What are you doing?

388
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,080
Zhou Fang isn't back.

389
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,400
Who asked about him?

390
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:28,440
You're still pretending with me?

391
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,200
Are you going to let me read or what?

392
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,240
Bro.

393
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,880
Did something happen to Joy Bells?

394
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,800
Zhou Fang didn't tell you?

395
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,480
You've got some nerve, Zhou Fang.

396
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:11,240
I thought you'd already cut ties with your dad.

397
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:13,480
I didn't expect you to give up at the first sign of trouble.

398
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:15,040
And to think I actually wanted to help you.

399
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:16,840
I'm such an idiot.

400
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,360
Wumei.

401
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,200
Get in touch with Mr. He again tomorrow.

402
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:31,280
Mr. He? I'm afraid our chances are slim.

403
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:32,520
Dad.

404
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,680
Mr. Zhou, what brings you here?

405
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,360
I heard you can't even pay your suppliers.

406
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,240
I thought it was a joke.

407
00:22:58,280 --> 00:22:59,560
But it turns out it's true.

408
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:02,080
Honest to God.

409
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:03,680
I really didn't say anything this time.

410
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,120
I came here on my own.

411
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:06,840
Don't blame him.

412
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:08,840
Go make some tea.

413
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,040
Okay, Mr. Zhou.

414
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,520
Dad.

415
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,880
If you came all the way here just to mock me...

416
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:21,400
Can't you talk to your dad nicely?

417
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,160
At the end of the day,

418
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,000
the initial funding for Joy Bells

419
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,960
came from me.

420
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:29,040
So the fact that I haven't bankrupted Joy Bells yet,

421
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:31,600
must be really disappointing to you.

422
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:35,160
Do you think with your abilities,

423
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,480
you can still hold on?

424
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:38,040
The ship is falling apart,

425
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:39,280
yet you insist on setting sail.

426
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:40,880
It's my ship,

427
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:44,080
and I'll make sure it sails.

428
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:46,000
The problem is you don't even have fuel.

429
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,320
How are you going to sail?

430
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:53,840
Zhou Fang.

431
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:56,440
Look at the state you're in.

432
00:23:56,720 --> 00:23:58,280
What can you give Chen Xiaofang?

433
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:00,880
She loves money more than anything.

434
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,640
Would she board your sinking ship?

435
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,480
Dad.

436
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,160
Do you really understand love?

437
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,160
You're just a businessman.

438
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:11,680
A businessman who only cares about money.

439
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:14,480
If you understood love even a little bit,

440
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:18,400
would our relationship be like this now?

441
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:23,320
My relationship with Xiaofang is none of your business.

442
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:27,680
And I will keep Joy Bells running smoothly.

443
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:31,400
When you can't even afford to eat,

444
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,560
love doesn't mean shit.

445
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:38,760
I'm done talking to you.

446
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,040
When you figure things out,

447
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,640
come back to me.

448
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:47,360
Mr. Zhou,

449
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:48,200
leaving so soon?

450
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:49,960
The tea is just ready.

451
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:50,600
I'll pass.

452
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,640
I'm sorry. Give me some time.

453
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:07,560
Once I build a future you can rely on,

454
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,560
I'll come back to you.

455
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:27,760
Chen Xiaofang.

456
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:32,320
Mr. Zhou.

457
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:34,560
You're a businessman.

458
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,880
You should at least keep your word.

459
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:39,160
You took my money,

460
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:40,840
so you should do as you promised.

461
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:43,840
What do you mean?

462
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:45,520
Because of you, Zhou Fang

463
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:47,640
has completely fallen out

464
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,200
with me, his own father.

465
00:25:58,560 --> 00:25:59,360
Mr. Zhou,

466
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:01,000
as for your money,

467
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,040
I haven't touched a single cent.

468
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:06,000
What do you mean?

469
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:11,320
When you gave me that one million,

470
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:14,200
you put a price tag on my marriage to your son.

471
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:17,600
But now,

472
00:26:18,560 --> 00:26:19,960
I don't think one million is enough.

473
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:22,960
No amount you give me would be enough.

474
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:25,560
Because I love him.

475
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:29,360
All this time,

476
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,280
Zhou Fang has followed your orders

477
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:33,560
to be a good, obedient son.

478
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:37,360
But have you ever considered what he really wants?

479
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:41,960
Now, he makes his own decisions.

480
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:44,240
He takes responsibility for his employees.

481
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,680
And he takes care of his family.

482
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:49,160
Can't you see

483
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:50,920
how much he's grown?

484
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:58,840
Please wait, Mr. Zhou.

485
00:27:05,120 --> 00:27:06,120
This card...

486
00:27:06,120 --> 00:27:08,280
I think when the day comes

487
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:10,480
that Zhou Fang truly makes you proud,

488
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:14,440
you can use it as your blessing

489
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:15,680
and give it back to me.

490
00:27:49,560 --> 00:27:50,720
Damn it!

491
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:53,240
Zhou Fang, you son of a bitch!

492
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:54,920
Teaming up with your Pops to piss me off!

493
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,080
Old Wu

494
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,240
Why are you here?

495
00:28:13,840 --> 00:28:15,120
Have you eaten yet?

496
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:16,640
I brought you some food.

497
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,120
I haven't eaten yet.

498
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:21,760
Food is fuel, you know.

499
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:23,360
How can you go without eating?

500
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:25,440
That's very thoughtful, Old Wu.

501
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:31,040
I know the company has had some issues lately.

502
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:32,160
But don't worry.

503
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:34,480
I will always stand by you.

504
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:38,960
Sister Lan.

505
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:41,320
It's a shame you don't open a restaurant with your skills.

506
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:42,920
Just eat your food.

507
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:44,080
And stop talking nonsense.

508
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:47,080
Boss Zhou.

509
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:50,040
There's a favor I'd like to ask you.

510
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:54,240
Yiran's birthday is coming up in a few days.

511
00:28:54,800 --> 00:28:55,600
As you know,

512
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:59,040
I haven't celebrated her birthday for years.

513
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:00,720
I originally wanted to book

514
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:03,360
the restaurant where Xiaofu held his banquet.

515
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:04,720
But it's too hard to book.

516
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:07,000
Okay, I'll call and book it for you now.

517
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Thank you. Thanks a lot.

518
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,520
Leave some for others.

519
00:29:14,520 --> 00:29:15,480
Your mouth

520
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:17,240
is only good for talking nonsense and eating.

521
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:19,400
It's just so delicious!

522
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:21,400
Just one last piece.

523
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:24,480
Old Wu.

524
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:26,200
I've made the call for you.

525
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:28,120
It's booked. I got you the biggest private room.

526
00:29:28,360 --> 00:29:29,560
Thanks, Boss Zhou.

527
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:31,120
Zhou Fang, get the hell out here!

528
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:34,760
Xiaofang.

529
00:29:34,760 --> 00:29:36,120
Zhou Fang!

530
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:38,240
You, get over to me!

531
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:39,040
Xiao...

532
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:40,240
Why are you here, Xiaofang?

533
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:41,120
Zhou Fang,

534
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,720
did you think by blocking me,

535
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:43,800
your business would succeed?

536
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,320
Did you think by not contacting me,

537
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:46,440
you're being responsible?

538
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,760
If I were really after your money,

539
00:29:47,760 --> 00:29:49,120
I would've stopped contacting you.

540
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:50,240
I would've stopped contacting you long ago!

541
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:51,680
Xiaofang,

542
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:52,960
that's not what I meant.

543
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:53,680
You misunderstood me.

544
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:54,720
Give me a break.

545
00:29:56,840 --> 00:29:57,760
Chen Xiaofang.

546
00:29:58,280 --> 00:29:59,200
You misunderstood me.

547
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:00,600
I really didn't mean that.

548
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:01,600
Do you know what the most important thing is

549
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:02,720
when two people are together?

550
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:04,800
It's trust.

551
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:07,600
I know you want to do big things

552
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:08,920
and succeed on your own,

553
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:11,840
but have you ever considered my feelings?

554
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,240
The future, the future...

555
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:16,200
It's only a future if we support each other.

556
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,560
What is it when you're alone?

557
00:30:18,040 --> 00:30:19,720
Then why don't you just live alone?

558
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:23,360
Xiaofang,

559
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:25,320
I'm... I'm sorry.

560
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:30,000
I can give up everything in this world,

561
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:32,320
except you.

562
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,360
I don't care about anything else, except you.

563
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:58,120
I was wrong.

564
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:21,640
Still trying to jump?

565
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:23,560
You still can't reach even if you jump.

566
00:31:26,360 --> 00:31:27,320
You're tall.

567
00:31:27,320 --> 00:31:28,000
You're tall.

568
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:30,160
Tall or not, you still don't get to kiss me.

569
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:32,800
Let's go.

570
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:35,000
What are you doing in broad daylight?

571
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,040
What are you doing?

572
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:42,560
Nothing, nothing.

573
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:46,920
Xiaofang! Xiaofang!

574
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,920
What made you want to get your hair done today?

575
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:25,080
Isn't it Yiran's birthday?

576
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:29,880
Give me a style that's not too flashy,

577
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:32,240
but not too ordinary either.

578
00:32:32,320 --> 00:32:35,080
Just make it fit a mother's vibe.

579
00:32:35,080 --> 00:32:36,040
You know that kind of hairstyle.

580
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:37,880
You don't need to tell me that.

581
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:39,560
Don't you trust my skills?

582
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:42,280
You'll get a massive eye roll from me.

583
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:42,760
Did you forget

584
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:44,520
what you made me look like last time?

585
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:46,800
Zhang Lijuan!

586
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,120
You permed it for me,

587
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:50,280
saying it was the Marilyn Monroe look!

588
00:32:52,520 --> 00:32:53,320
Sister Lan,

589
00:32:53,320 --> 00:32:54,800
the curling iron broke.

590
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:56,640
So it's just me doing your hair today.

591
00:32:56,640 --> 00:32:58,440
Good that it's broken.

592
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:04,640
Time really flies.

593
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:07,000
The kids grew up in the blink of an eye.

594
00:33:07,160 --> 00:33:10,160
I still remember the first time Yiran got a haircut here.

595
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:12,840
She wanted a bob cut.

596
00:33:12,840 --> 00:33:14,240
Her long hair,

597
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:15,760
gone with just one snip.

598
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:16,880
She cried so hard.

599
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:19,040
I comforted her for half an hour, but it was no use.

600
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:20,880
She's loved looking pretty since she was little.

601
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:22,760
By the way,

602
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:25,000
I have a secret to tell you.

603
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:26,760
What is it?

604
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:32,040
I want to give Yiran a surprise.

605
00:33:32,040 --> 00:33:33,280
What kind of surprise?

606
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:06,440
Hello, Xiaoli.

607
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:09,080
Yes, yes, exactly.

608
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:12,120
My daughter is a very picky eater.

609
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:13,520
If you don't prepare it carefully,

610
00:34:13,520 --> 00:34:14,840
she won't eat anything at all.

611
00:34:15,080 --> 00:34:16,440
Right, right.

612
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:17,560
Thanks for your help.

613
00:34:17,560 --> 00:34:18,560
Make sure it's perfect.

614
00:34:18,560 --> 00:34:19,960
Otherwise she really won't eat.

615
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,280
Okay.

616
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:24,360
Wu Huilian.

617
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:26,440
Are you kidding me?

618
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:27,560
I'm not the Queen.

619
00:34:27,560 --> 00:34:28,840
Why make me sound so high-maintenance?

620
00:34:29,240 --> 00:34:31,280
Do you know how hard it is to book this restaurant?

621
00:34:31,480 --> 00:34:33,920
I even had our Boss Zhou book it for me.

622
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:36,320
It cost so much money, so it has to be perfect.

623
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,240
Right?

624
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:39,480
We have to do this in style.

625
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,520
You're really something.

626
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:42,040
You sure know how to handle people.

627
00:34:45,280 --> 00:34:46,320
Come here.

628
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:48,840
Mom made these especially for you.

629
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:50,040
Longevity noodles.

630
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:52,120
It smells so good.

631
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:53,600
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

632
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:56,160
Come on.

633
00:34:56,160 --> 00:34:57,520
Why are you just standing there?

634
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:58,000
Hurry up.

635
00:34:58,360 --> 00:34:58,920
Sit.

636
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:12,520
Thanks.

637
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:15,560
What are you thanking me for?

638
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,720
No need to be so polite with your mom.

639
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:20,320
Hurry up, try it.

640
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,000
Mix it up. Mix it up.

641
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:28,720
Wait a minute.

642
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:40,160
Birthday gift.

643
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:42,680
Thank you.

644
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,760
Why are you saying thank you again?

645
00:35:47,080 --> 00:35:47,880
Sweetie,

646
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:50,880
could you please

647
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:52,760
promise Mom one thing?

648
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:54,320
What?

649
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:55,920
Just promise me first, okay?

650
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:56,840
Fine.

651
00:35:58,280 --> 00:36:02,800
This is the birthday outfit Mom carefully prepared for you.

652
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:05,040
Once you put it on,

653
00:36:05,040 --> 00:36:08,160
you'll definitely blind everyone with your beauty.

654
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:15,040
So pretty.

655
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:17,560
You look just like a star from Hong Kong, China!

656
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:18,200
Beautiful!

657
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:19,960
I shouldn't have listened to you.

658
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:20,920
What is this?

659
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:22,520
Talk about blinding everyone...

660
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:23,960
you've completely blinded me!

661
00:36:25,720 --> 00:36:28,560
It's so pretty, how does it blind you?

662
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:29,880
It looks absolutely gorgeous!

663
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:30,880
It really does look good.

664
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:32,600
But there was no need to go this far.

665
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,080
What do I look like standing here?

666
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:35,240
Like a monkey in a show.

667
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:36,120
I'm not standing here anymore.

668
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:36,640
You stand here if you want.

669
00:36:36,640 --> 00:36:37,600
It's just a birthday,

670
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:38,440
not a wedding.

671
00:36:39,640 --> 00:36:40,520
Come back, come back!

672
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:42,280
Sweetie,

673
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:44,080
you'll have to get married eventually anyway.

674
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:45,480
Just treat this as a rehearsal.

675
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:46,400
You look so pretty.

676
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:47,720
Then I'm not wearing this.

677
00:36:47,720 --> 00:36:48,440
Hold it, hold it.

678
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:51,080
Yiran!

679
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:51,800
You coming here is enough,

680
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:52,800
why did you bring a gift?

681
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:54,160
Oh my god!

682
00:36:54,160 --> 00:36:55,880
You're dressed like a movie star today!

683
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,480
Absolutely beautiful!

684
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:58,840
Thanks to Auntie Juan for doing my hair.

685
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:00,600
Yiran,

686
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:01,640
may your grace bloom like orchids,

687
00:37:01,640 --> 00:37:02,480
and flourish year after year.

688
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:03,280
Happy birthday!

689
00:37:03,880 --> 00:37:05,000
Thank you, Brother Amin.

690
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:05,840
What Brother Amin?

691
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:06,560
It's Uncle Amin.

692
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:07,840
You're messing up the generations.

693
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,280
Thank you, Uncle Amin.

694
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:11,960
Yangyang is dressed so cutely today.

695
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:15,120
Don't hit Yiran.

696
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:16,120
Go on in, go on in.

697
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:16,600
Come on, Yangyang.

698
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:17,000
Go inside.

699
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:17,680
Come on.

700
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:19,360
Isn't Sister Yiran pretty?

701
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:19,880
Pretty.

702
00:37:23,120 --> 00:37:23,720
Yiran.

703
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:24,840
Happy birthday.

704
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:25,440
Uncle Chen!

705
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:26,480
Happy birthday.

706
00:37:26,960 --> 00:37:27,440
Thank you.

707
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:28,160
Take your time, take your time.

708
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:30,920
Great, great.

709
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:37,760
Does it look weird?

710
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:39,680
Not at all.

711
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:41,280
It looks great, really great.

712
00:37:42,600 --> 00:37:43,320
Brother Chen!

713
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,360
Welcome, welcome!

714
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:46,360
Hello, hello!

715
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:47,080
Happy birthday!

716
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:50,600
Step forward to hand over the gift!

717
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,240
This is so frustrating.

718
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:54,240
If he'd just taken a few more steps,

719
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,760
our families would be celebrating a double joy.

720
00:37:55,760 --> 00:37:56,320
Wu Huilian!

721
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,080
Am I wrong?

722
00:37:58,680 --> 00:37:59,880
Slow down, slow down.

723
00:38:01,480 --> 00:38:03,080
So, about this gift...

724
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:05,360
You actually bought a gift?

725
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:07,080
Yeah, it's your birthday.

726
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:08,880
Then help me carry it inside.

727
00:38:09,760 --> 00:38:10,280
Sure.

728
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:19,400
Beautiful.

729
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:20,600
Xiaofang.

730
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,800
How are you so pretty?

731
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:22,800
Thank you.

732
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,080
Here, happy birthday.

733
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:24,560
Thanks.

734
00:38:24,960 --> 00:38:25,840
Help me take it inside.

735
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:26,240
Sure, sure.

736
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:26,800
Thank you.

737
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:28,000
I know you like practical things.

738
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:30,160
Remember to accept the transfer.

739
00:38:30,520 --> 00:38:32,360
Boss Chen is so generous.

740
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,200
Go inside and take a seat.

741
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:33,920
Let's go, let's go.

742
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:34,560
What did you just say?

743
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:35,640
We got the project.

744
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:36,160
Really?

745
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:36,520
Yeah.

746
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:37,560
You're here.

747
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:38,680
Old Wu.

748
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:40,000
Go inside and sit down, hurry.

749
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:40,800
Alright.

750
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:43,120
The room looks great.

751
00:38:45,840 --> 00:38:47,640
Why isn't Uncle Daren here yet?

752
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:49,520
Did you tell him what time to come?

753
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:51,160
Of course I did.

754
00:38:51,160 --> 00:38:52,680
Sorry, sorry.

755
00:38:52,680 --> 00:38:53,200
Uncle Daren.

756
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:53,720
I'm late.

757
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,000
Happy birthday, Yiran.

758
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:57,480
Thanks, Uncle Daren.

759
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:58,280
You're all sweaty.

760
00:38:58,280 --> 00:38:59,160
You're right on time.

761
00:38:59,160 --> 00:38:59,400
Let's go.

762
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,200
Sorry.

763
00:39:00,200 --> 00:39:00,920
I'm late.

764
00:39:01,120 --> 00:39:01,960
Not at all.

765
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:03,240
Go inside and have some water.

766
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,160
Okay, sure.

767
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,120
Yiran.

768
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:21,840
Why are you spacing out? Hurry up.

769
00:39:27,840 --> 00:39:29,240
You look so pretty today.

770
00:39:32,760 --> 00:39:35,480
Happy birthday to you

771
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:38,520
Happy birthday to you

772
00:39:38,520 --> 00:39:41,600
Happy birthday to you

773
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:44,840
Happy birthday to you

774
00:39:48,080 --> 00:39:49,520
Thank you, everyone.

775
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,200
Thank you.

776
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,760
It's too early for that.

777
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:56,520
I have another surprise for you.

778
00:39:57,120 --> 00:39:57,480
Juanzi,

779
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:58,200
bring it here.

780
00:40:01,080 --> 00:40:01,960
Auntie Huilian,

781
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,400
is this a family heirloom or what?

782
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:07,320
Pretty much.

783
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:09,360
Here.

784
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:12,480
Hold out both hands.

785
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:21,400
I sold the old house,

786
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:22,760
added some money,

787
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:24,160
and paid a down payment.

788
00:40:24,160 --> 00:40:26,440
Don't worry about the mortgage from now on.

789
00:40:26,600 --> 00:40:27,480
I'll pay it.

790
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:30,760
You have a new house now.

791
00:40:36,960 --> 00:40:37,920
What did you say?

792
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:42,080
Who told you to sell the house?

793
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:45,400
I... I... I...

794
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:45,920
We...

795
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:49,640
We've lived in that old house for decades.

796
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:52,880
I just thought we should get a new one.

797
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:55,800
You'll get married eventually anyway,

798
00:40:56,040 --> 00:40:58,240
so consider it a dowry from Mom.

799
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,720
Why would you do something this big

800
00:40:59,720 --> 00:41:01,120
without even discussing it with me?

801
00:41:01,240 --> 00:41:02,400
It's not just a house.

802
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:04,080
That's the home Pops left for me.

803
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:06,440
As long as I live there, I feel like Pops is still here.

804
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:08,440
What gave you the right to just sell it?

805
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:16,280
Yiran.

806
00:41:17,080 --> 00:41:17,800
Yiran.

807
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:19,680
Don't get upset. Take it easy.

808
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:21,200
Your mom means well.

809
00:41:21,200 --> 00:41:22,440
Exactly, Yiran.

810
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:24,960
It wasn't easy for your mom to save up all those years.

811
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:26,840
Isn't this for your own good?

812
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:29,040
If you don't like it,

813
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:30,520
I'll go and return it.

814
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:31,600
Wu Huilian,

815
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:33,760
you have no idea what I like

816
00:41:33,760 --> 00:41:34,840
or what I'm afraid of.

817
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:37,080
You don't know what I want.

818
00:41:41,480 --> 00:41:42,520
I... I just thought

819
00:41:42,520 --> 00:41:46,360
we'd lived in that house for so many years.

820
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:48,920
I didn't want you to be trapped in there forever.

821
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:49,800
Right?

822
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,720
We always have to look forward in life.

823
00:41:51,720 --> 00:41:52,280
Come on.

824
00:41:52,280 --> 00:41:52,920
Yeah, yeah.

825
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:53,600
Come on, come on.

826
00:41:53,600 --> 00:41:54,160
Let's have a drink.

827
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,200
It's a birthday.

828
00:41:56,040 --> 00:41:56,600
Right.

829
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:59,120
Wu Huilian.

830
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:03,320
From the very beginning, the one trapping me is you.

831
00:42:05,720 --> 00:42:06,760
It's you!

832
00:42:08,840 --> 00:42:09,320
Yiran.

833
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:09,840
Yiran!

834
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:10,400
Yiran!

835
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:11,760
Auntie Lan, I'll go talk to her.

836
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:17,640
It's fine, it's fine.

837
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:18,480
Have a seat. Have a seat.

838
00:42:18,480 --> 00:42:19,560
Don't take it to heart.

839
00:42:19,560 --> 00:42:21,280
That child, Yiran...

840
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:22,560
She just has a stubborn temper.

841
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:23,960
About what happened today,

842
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:25,800
you were indeed in the wrong.

843
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:28,400
Pops...

844
00:42:30,040 --> 00:42:31,440
Brother Chen, Brother Chen...

845
00:42:33,640 --> 00:42:34,480
It's my fault.

846
00:42:36,080 --> 00:42:37,680
I really...

847
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:39,520
just don't know what she actually likes.

848
00:42:46,120 --> 00:42:46,800
Yiran.

849
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:47,800
Yiran!

850
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:51,000
Yiran, you... just calm down.

851
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:52,440
I can't calm down!

852
00:42:52,920 --> 00:42:54,640
We can talk about this properly.

853
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:57,200
There was no need to embarrass Auntie Lan in front of so many people.

854
00:42:58,320 --> 00:42:59,120
Fine.

855
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:00,760
I was wrong.

856
00:43:01,400 --> 00:43:02,280
It's my fault.

857
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,560
It's all my fault, okay?

858
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:04,280
I... I didn't...

859
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,360
I... I didn't mean it that way.

860
00:43:05,360 --> 00:43:06,640
I didn't mean it that way.

861
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:07,640
I just wanted to tell you that

862
00:43:07,640 --> 00:43:08,920
once some words are spoken,

863
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,440
they... they can't be taken back.

864
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:11,360
Do you understand?

865
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:14,240
But she didn't even discuss it with me.

866
00:43:15,120 --> 00:43:16,880
She just sold my home.

867
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:19,480
Sold my memories.

868
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:22,040
Sold the only keepsake Pops left me.

869
00:43:22,040 --> 00:43:22,840
What gives her the right?

870
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:24,800
Did she even consider my feelings?

871
00:43:24,800 --> 00:43:27,400
Yes, Auntie Lan didn't think this through.

872
00:43:28,120 --> 00:43:29,520
But those things you said just now, you...

873
00:43:30,520 --> 00:43:31,680
you really crossed the line.

874
00:43:32,320 --> 00:43:34,320
Why are you defending her, too?

875
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:40,400
You've never watched your Pops die right in front of you.

876
00:43:41,480 --> 00:43:43,680
Or been bullied and laughed at.

877
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:46,240
Let alone having a mom who killed someone and went to jail.

878
00:43:49,520 --> 00:43:50,520
So,

879
00:43:53,120 --> 00:43:55,280
what gives you the right to lecture me now?

880
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:03,080
Yiran! Yiran!

881
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:26,000
Yiran

882
00:44:40,880 --> 00:44:42,160
This house,

883
00:44:42,160 --> 00:44:44,360
if you don't want to sell it,

884
00:44:44,760 --> 00:44:46,120
we don't have to.

885
00:44:46,880 --> 00:44:49,040
I'll go find the buyer tomorrow

886
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:50,920
and just return his deposit.

887
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:52,680
At worst, we just lose some money.

888
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:56,280
I can cancel the new house too.

889
00:45:00,560 --> 00:45:02,520
Please don't be mad anymore, okay?

890
00:45:04,520 --> 00:45:05,800
Mom was wrong.

891
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:41,360
Who is it?

892
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:42,600
Sister Lan.

893
00:45:43,720 --> 00:45:44,600
It's me.

894
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:20,960
Hongyu
